# QUIT — Incomplete Analysis (3.6) — Corrected Plan

**Severity:** Error | **Category:** IncompleteAnalysis | **can_be_disabled:** false
**Official message:** "Code analysis did not complete. Code Analyzer encountered an error."

## Key architectural change
QUIT is NOT a parse-pattern check. It is an **engine panic guard**: if the linter encounters an internal error (a panic) while analyzing a file, it reports QUIT instead of crashing. Implement in `Linter::lint` (`crates/mlt_core/src/linter.rs`) via `std::panic::catch_unwind`.

